---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About · Nova"
  description="How Nova builds a personal AI teammate that people can understand and control."
>
  <div class="container">
    <Header />
    <main id="main" class="privacy-copy">
      <h1>About Nova</h1>
      <p>
        Nova is a personal AI teammate: bots that can use a browser and shell,
        remember the work around a job, run routines on a schedule, and ask for approval when they reach a
        boundary. It is designed for practical operational work rather than one-off chat.
      </p>
      <h2>Why we are building it</h2>
      <p>
        Useful agents should be understandable and controllable by the people who run them. Nova keeps
        routines in readable Markdown, supports multiple model providers, records actions in an audit log, and
        lets operators keep model keys, browser sessions, and deployment infrastructure under their own
        control. The same bots and routines work across the web, desktop, and mobile clients.
      </p>
      <h2>Self-hostable</h2>
      <p>
        Nova is a private, closed product. To run Nova on your own
        infrastructure, email <a href="mailto:hello@nova.example">hello@nova.example</a> for setup help. For product or account help,
        email <a href="mailto:hello@nova.example">hello@nova.example</a>.
      </p>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
